{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfS5uMFY1d71W58DAZsWt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 03 is done and everything is written. Nothing remains that the driver needs from me.\n\n**Outcome.** 5,646 of the 6,135 certified corpus instances at 9–40 customers now carry a DRAT refutation of `optimum − 1` that drat-trim verifies from the DIMACS alone. That is 92.0%, with zero checker rejections, zero contradicted optima, and zero wall-deadline kills. The 489 left all exhausted a million CaDiCaL conflicts.\n\n**What was built**\n- `tools/drat-trim/`: Heule's checker vendored from its public source and built with `gnu99`, since the upstream `c99` flag fails on this glibc. Provenance in `tools/README.md`.\n- `learning/proofs.py`: applies the two `decide_mosp` reductions and records them as index lists, solves with CaDiCaL under a conflict budget inside a killable child, checks with drat-trim, stores compressed proofs plus JSON certificates under the git-ignored `learning/data/proofs/`, and commits one row per instance to `learning/data/proofs.csv`. A `check` stage rebuilds the CNF from the benchmark file and certificate alone and re-verifies.\n- `tests/test_proofs.py`: seven tests, including the 4-customer proof checking and four corruptions failing. Full suite: 900 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n\n**Two pysat facts that shaped the design.** `interrupt()` raises `NotImplementedError` for CaDiCaL, so the first batch's deadline was never enforced and it was stopped and discarded. `get_proof()` returns a truncated proof because pysat never flushes the C trace buffer. A `libc.fflush(NULL)` before reading the trace gives complete proofs.\n\n**Finding, in one line.** Affordability is decided by the formula size `m²·k`, not by `n`: zero censoring below 5,000, then 4%, 25%, 69% per decade, every instance with at most 20 patterns certified at any width, and the first failures at 200k conflicts are at `n = 10`. The proof costs 6,000 to 70,000 times the customer search's seconds on the same questions, so it is an archive object, not a decision procedure, and the encoding has nothing to offer at 125×125.\n\n**Files for the driver to commit.** `learning/proofs.py`, `tests/test_proofs.py`, `tools/`, `.gitignore`, `reports/ml_nature.md` §17, `reports/proof_tables.md`, `learning/data/proofs.csv`, `learning/data/proofs_200k.csv`, PROGRESS.md and iterations.md. Nothing under `solutions/` changed. The cost was 13 core-hours across the two passes, and 11.7 GB of proofs sit on disk outside git."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":714,"cache_read_input_tokens":238525,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":714,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":756,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bd98a571-ecf9-476d-b54f-657dcce8d941","uuid":"bde3ed48-48cb-49a0-9483-381e73e6840e","timestamp":"2026-09-26T12:54:49.246Z","request_id":"req_011CfS5uLQwXkKN2hwoMaqJt"}
